    "intro_html":  "Yassa is proof that onions are the most underrated ingredient in the grocery store. Six pounds of them cook down into something jammy and almost sweet, sharpened with lemon and dijon mustard, with chicken braised right in the middle of it. Senegal has been making this dish for generations and the ingredient list has barely changed, because it did not need to. Each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) served over rice.",
